WHY THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC

  It is public for two practical reasons and no others: the privacy policy, support page and
  terms the App Store requires are served from it through GitHub Pages, and the work is
  published so that it can be read, linked to and discussed. Being able to read something is
  not permission to use it, and a public repository is not an offer of a licence.

PERMITTED WITHOUT PERMISSION

  1. Reading the Work.
  2. Quoting short excerpts for commentary, teaching, review or discussion, with attribution
     to the copyright holder and a link to this repository.
  3. Forking on the hosting platform in order to propose a change back to this repository.
     A fork is a copy the platform makes; it is not a licence to use what is in it.

NOT PERMITTED WITHOUT PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION

  1. Copying any part of the Work into another project, by any means: by hand, by file, by
     rewriting it in another language, or by having a machine do any of those.
  2. Using the Work, in whole or in part, in any product, service or application, whether
     commercial or not, whether published or private.
  3. Modifying, merging, publishing, distributing, sublicensing, selling or renting the Work
     or any copy of it.
  4. Publishing or distributing any application derived from, or substantially similar to,
     the Work on any application store or distribution channel.
  5. Using the name "Sunspot", the icon, the screenshots or the wording of the screens for
     any application other than this one.
  6. Training machine-learning models on the Work.

  This list describes what is refused most often. It is not exhaustive: every right that is
  not expressly granted above is reserved.

